# Allowlist model: ignore EVERYTHING, then un-ignore only what the
# repo-root-context builds (the system images via
# deploy/docker/system-images.Dockerfile) actually COPY. This keeps the build
# context to a few MB of source instead of the whole tree (target/ alone is many
# GB), and it stays correct when new heavy dirs appear (they are ignored by
# default, never dragged in). The builder base does NOT build from the repo
# root: it uses the staged `.weft-base-context/` dir as its own context.
#
# The system-images Dockerfile COPYs: rust-toolchain.toml, Cargo.toml,
# Cargo.lock, crates/, catalog/. deploy/ is kept so the Dockerfile referenced
# with `-f` is inside the context too.
*

!rust-toolchain.toml
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!crates/
!catalog/
!deploy/

# Even inside the allowlisted dirs, never ship build artifacts or VCS/dev junk.
**/target/
**/node_modules/
**/.svelte-kit/
**/pkg/
.git/
**/.env
**/*.db
**/*.db-journal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
